# CRITICAL DATABASE SAFETY RULES

## NEVER TOUCH PRODUCTION DATABASE
- NEVER run commands on /home/ubuntu/datatracker/instance/datatracker.db
- NEVER copy, move, or modify instance/datatracker.db
- NEVER run migrations on production without explicit user confirmation
- ALWAYS work in development: instance_dev/datatracker_dev.db
- ALWAYS use FLASK_ENV=development

## Before ANY database operation:
1. Confirm which environment (dev vs prod)
2. Create timestamped backup FIRST
3. Verify backup has data before proceeding
4. Get explicit user approval for production changes

## Development workflow:
- Use: instance_dev/datatracker_dev.db
- Set: FLASK_ENV=development
- Port: 5000 (not 8000)

## Production is READ-ONLY unless user explicitly says:
"modify production database" or "run migration on production"

If production shows 0 documents or unexpected state:
- STOP
- ASK USER
- DO NOT "fix" it by copying data
